# Naming Conventions

This project enforces naming standards at the level of an obsessive Apple engineer. Every identifier must read as if it came from a first-party Apple framework.

## Core Principle

Names must be clear at the point of use. Read every call site as a prose sentence — if it sounds unnatural or requires a comment to understand, rename it.

## Allowed Abbreviations

Only abbreviations that Apple itself uses in its public frameworks are permitted:

- `x`, `xx`, `xxx`, `xxxx` as size-scale prefixes — `xSmall`, `xxLarge` (`DynamicTypeSize` pattern)
- `URL`, `UUID`, `HTTP`, `JSON`, `XML`, `HTML`, `API`, `ID` — established acronyms used as full words
- `max`, `min` — universally understood

Everything else must be spelled out in full.

## Forbidden Abbreviations

The following (and anything like them) are strictly banned:

`btn`, `lbl`, `img`, `str`, `num`, `val`, `obj`, `vc`, `nav`, `cfg`, `mgr`, `ctx`, `err`, `cb`, `fn`, `tmp`, `res`, `req`, `resp`, `auth`, `coord`, `attr`, `param`, `msg`, `notif`, `anim`, `perf`, `ref`

## Rules by Identifier Type

### Types (class, struct, enum, protocol, typealias)
- Use nouns or noun phrases: `MapAnnotation`, `PlaceDetail`, `AuthenticationState`
- No generic suffixes: never `PlaceManager`, `ListHelper`, `DataUtility`
- Protocol naming:
  - Capability → `-able` / `-ible`: `Identifiable`, `Equatable`
  - Description → noun: `Collection`, `View`, `Shape`

### Functions and Methods
- Start with a verb: `fetchPlace()`, `saveList()`, `updateAnnotation()`
- Parameters read as natural English at the call site:
  - Good: `move(pin:to:)` → `move(pin: annotation, to: coordinate)`
  - Bad: `movePinToCoord(pin:coord:)` → reads as jargon
- Omit needless words but never at the cost of clarity

### Properties
- Use nouns or noun phrases: `placeName`, `savedLists`, `selectedCategory`
- Booleans use `is`, `has`, `should`, `can`, `needs`:
  - `isLoading`, `hasUnsavedChanges`, `shouldShowOnboarding`, `canEdit`
- Never: `loading`, `unsavedChanges`, `showOnboarding`

### Enum Cases
- `lowerCamelCase`: `.backgroundBrand`, `.titleSmall`, `.xLarge`
- No type name repetition: `Radius.large` not `Radius.radiusLarge`

### Constants and Variables
- `lowerCamelCase` throughout
- Static constants in enums are the preferred token pattern for design system values

## File Naming
- One primary type per file, file name matches the type: `PlaceDetailView.swift`, `DesignSystem.swift`
- No `Helpers.swift`, `Utils.swift`, `Extensions.swift` catch-all files — scope extensions to their subject: `Color+Hex.swift`
